{{!--
    A horizontal shelf of posts for one tag.

    Driven by the homepage_shelf_tags setting — a comma-separated list of tag
    slugs. This partial renders one shelf; home.hbs decides how many there are.

    Two Ghost quirks meet in this file, and they pull in opposite directions.

    {{#get}} invokes its body with the API response as the context. So inside the
    inner query, a bare {{name}} resolves against that response and comes out
    empty — the shelf headings render blank. Block parameters are lexically
    scoped and survive the switch, which is why the heading reads
    {{shelfTag.name}}.

    But a {{#get}} `filter` string is resolved against the *context*, by Ghost's
    own path resolver, which cannot see block parameters at all. So the filter
    has to use the bare {{slug}} from the surrounding foreach.

    Hence the apparent inconsistency below: block parameter for display, plain
    context path inside the filter. Both are required, and swapping either one
    fails silently.

    The row is a scroll container, so it is focusable and labelled — cards past
    the edge have to stay reachable by keyboard, which a carousel with hidden
    slides would not be.

    Parameters
      slug   the tag to draw from (required)
--}}
{{#get "tags" filter="slug:{{slug}}" limit="1" as |shelfTags|}}
    {{#foreach shelfTags as |shelfTag|}}
        {{#get "posts" filter="tag:{{slug}}" limit="8" include="authors,tags" as |shelfPosts|}}
            <section class="ghost-shelf">
                <div class="ghost-container">
                    <div class="ghost-shelf__head">
                        <h2 class="ghost-shelf__title">{{shelfTag.name}}</h2>
                        <a class="ghost-shelf__more" href="{{shelfTag.url}}">
                            All {{shelfTag.name}} {{> "icon" name="arrow-right"}}
                        </a>
                    </div>

                    <ul class="ghost-shelf__track" tabindex="0" aria-label="{{shelfTag.name}} posts, scrollable">
                        {{#foreach shelfPosts}}
                            <li class="ghost-shelf__item">{{> "card"}}</li>
                        {{/foreach}}
                    </ul>
                </div>
            </section>
        {{/get}}
    {{/foreach}}
{{/get}}
